Lab: Implementing Basic Authentication and Data Encryption in Apache Camel Routes
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Implement HTTP Basic Authentication to secure Apache Camel REST routes using Spring Security
Configure role-based authorization so different endpoints require different user roles
Encrypt and decrypt sensitive data within a Camel route using AES encryption
Test secured routes with curl to verify authentication, authorization, and data privacy
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts and REST route building
Familiarity with REST API concepts and HTTP protocols
Basic knowledge of authentication and authorization principles
Experience with the Maven build tool
Basic Linux command-line skills
